ances, puzzled philosophers, lured collectors, and frightened the devout. Drawing on the histories of art, science, philosophy, and literature, Lorraine Daston and Katharine Park explore and explain how wonder and wonders fortified princely power, rewove the texture of scientific experience, and shaped the sensibility of intellectuals. This is a history of the passions of inquiry, of how wonder sometimes inflamed, sometimes dampened curiosity about nature’s best-kept secrets.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-wonders-and-the-order-of-nature-1150-1750-lorraine-daston-and-katharine-park.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.062,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0.356,"traits":[{"id":"essayistic","score":1,"confidence":"high","evidence":["catalog text contains \"essay\"","catalog text contains \"essays\"","catalog text contains \"criticism\"","literature/criticism subject or topic"]},{"id":"academic","score":0.38,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Princeton University Press / Princeton University Press"]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.32,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"story of\"","catalog text contains \"stories of\""]},{"id":"scholarly","score":0.28,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Princeton University Press / Princeton University Press"]},{"id":"synthesis","score":0.2,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"from\"","catalog text contains \"history of\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"From the High Middle Ages through the Enlightenment, European naturalists used wonder and its objects to reshape scientific experience—fortifying princely power and modulating curiosity about nature.","confidence":0.62},"academicOrientation":{"score":70,"confidence":0.55},"profileConfidence":0.72,"model":"gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17","promptVersion"